{
  "_about": [
    "Where props go (WLD-12). Each group is anchored to a landmark or Waystone from layout.json.",
    "'at' is [east, north] in meters from the anchor. 'facing' is the compass direction the prop's",
    "front looks toward (0 = north, 90 = east). 'line' repeats a prop end to end from 'from' to 'to'",
    "('gate_at' puts the gate prop at that fraction of the line). 'scatter' places props at random",
    "in a ring around the anchor, keeping off roads, steep ground and other props; 'scale' sizes each copy,",
    "'stretch' scales only its height (tall/slim vs squat variants of one model); 'groves': [n, radius]",
    "clusters them around n random grove centers instead. 'shore' scatters props along rivers and lakes",
    "(dry ground within reach_m of the water, plus the shallows) within 'radius' of the anchor.",
    "'ground' paints loose material on the terrain in ragged patches: {material, at, r} (material: hay).",
    "Nothing is placed on a path or road; 'path_ok': true allows it for places a path leads to",
    "(the well in the square, a cottage at the end of its doorstep path). Fence and wall lines leave gaps."
  ],
